1264
00:54:59.720 --> 00:54:59.840
I know.

1265
00:54:59.880 --> 00:55:04.260
Because I'm imagining Kelly's reaction when she hugs him, and it's just so funny.

1266
00:55:04.440 --> 00:55:05.700
She says, ew.

1267
00:55:05.760 --> 00:55:07.720
And he goes, you don't have to make that noise.

1268
00:55:07.740 --> 00:55:10.860
And she said, he was just so much bonier than I thought.

1269
00:55:11.040 --> 00:55:12.060
There's so many more bones.

1270
00:55:12.800 --> 00:55:18.400
When Gabe left, as I was watching it, I thought, this group of people can't wait to have a cake,

1271
00:55:18.560 --> 00:55:20.040
a party, for any reason.

1272
00:55:20.040 --> 00:55:22.000
And they literally are like, oh, what?

1273
00:55:22.040 --> 00:55:22.400
You're leaving?

1274
00:55:22.540 --> 00:55:22.840
Okay, bye.

1275
00:55:23.400 --> 00:55:24.080
I know.

1276
00:55:24.220 --> 00:55:27.680
And you can't even use the excuse that it all came down in one day.

1277
00:55:28.140 --> 00:55:31.400
Although maybe you can use the excuse that it's because Michael wasn't there.

1278
00:55:31.740 --> 00:55:36.360
Because even if someone's leaving in three hours, Michael's going to find a way to have

1279
00:55:36.360 --> 00:55:37.240
it to do about it.

1280
00:55:37.360 --> 00:55:37.520
Right.

1281
00:55:37.520 --> 00:55:41.300
So things have changed, especially when they're Gabe.

1282
00:55:42.200 --> 00:55:45.320
Jim is going to suggest Daryl again.

1283
00:55:45.700 --> 00:55:48.920
And this is when Angela decides to join the conversation.

1284
00:55:49.540 --> 00:55:52.180
She says, well, let me be clear.

1285
00:55:52.320 --> 00:55:56.680
I only speak for myself and not myself and the senator.

1286
00:55:57.160 --> 00:56:02.060
I think we have some wonderful candidates and there's a great, lively debate here.

1287
00:56:02.220 --> 00:56:03.620
But let's think about...

1288
00:56:03.620 --> 00:56:05.000
And Toby goes, no, no, no.

1289
00:56:05.140 --> 00:56:06.020
We did this with Kevin.

1290
00:56:06.180 --> 00:56:08.360
If you have nothing to say, stop talking.

1291
00:56:09.040 --> 00:56:09.860
So here's the thing.

1292
00:56:09.920 --> 00:56:14.300
When we started filming this scene, I talked to Paul and our director, Jeff Blitz, and

1293
00:56:14.300 --> 00:56:19.020
we had this idea that it would be really fun if Angela is already seeing herself as the

1294
00:56:19.020 --> 00:56:21.460
senator's wife and she's like on the campaign trail.

1295
00:56:21.460 --> 00:56:27.520
So she's practicing her campaign speeches, but she just decides to try it out right here.

1296
00:56:27.820 --> 00:56:31.320
And once they gave me that note, it was so much fun.

1297
00:56:31.520 --> 00:56:34.000
I couldn't wait to deliver these lines.

1298
00:56:34.240 --> 00:56:36.380
I love as an actor when you get a good note.

1299
00:56:36.660 --> 00:56:37.020
Yeah.

1300
00:56:37.380 --> 00:56:39.340
It changed the whole speech for me.

1301
00:56:39.340 --> 00:56:40.680
It opens up your whole performance.

1302
00:56:41.340 --> 00:56:43.540
Lady, we got a fan mail flurry.

1303
00:56:44.200 --> 00:56:48.360
It's really been a while since we've had such a flurry of mail on a single subject.

1304
00:56:48.520 --> 00:56:49.620
And it was this.

1305
00:56:49.620 --> 00:56:52.540
Why doesn't Jim step in as manager?

1306
00:56:52.860 --> 00:56:56.180
Why was he not considered or interviewed for the position?

1307
00:56:56.700 --> 00:56:58.120
He didn't want to be.

1308
00:56:58.300 --> 00:57:00.760
He didn't want to be interim manager.

1309
00:57:01.220 --> 00:57:09.320
But of everyone in the office besides Daryl, Jim is our other most sober, most qualified

1310
00:57:09.320 --> 00:57:09.940
candidate.

1311
00:57:10.540 --> 00:57:12.240
It is sort of a why.

1312
00:57:12.460 --> 00:57:17.940
Why doesn't he want a promotion with more money and more financial stability for his family?

1313
00:57:18.160 --> 00:57:19.100
Why doesn't he want that?

1314
00:57:19.620 --> 00:57:21.360
I agree with this fan mail flurry.

1315
00:57:21.580 --> 00:57:22.100
I don't know.

1316
00:57:22.460 --> 00:57:28.040
I think that the honest answer to this question is that they had no intention of making the

1317
00:57:28.040 --> 00:57:35.960
character of Jim the manager because the show isn't served by having a qualified, sober-minded

1318
00:57:35.960 --> 00:57:36.520
manager.

1319
00:57:37.120 --> 00:57:42.480
The whole show depends on having a branch manager that everyone doesn't like or has to deal with.

1320
00:57:42.840 --> 00:57:43.040
Correct.

1321
00:57:43.460 --> 00:57:46.940
Well, they're going to have to go back to the conference room now to figure this out.

1322
00:57:47.240 --> 00:57:52.440
Did any of you guys notice that Brian as Kevin follows them back in the conference room and they

1323
00:57:52.440 --> 00:57:53.540
shut the door in his face?

1324
00:57:53.740 --> 00:57:54.000
Yes.

1325
00:57:54.420 --> 00:57:55.740
Brian improvised that.

1326
00:57:55.740 --> 00:57:56.640
Oh, that's funny.

1327
00:57:56.820 --> 00:58:00.540
I totally remember him doing it in the moment and I was cracking up because I was like,

1328
00:58:00.600 --> 00:58:01.220
where's he going?

1329
00:58:02.100 --> 00:58:04.540
Well, we're going to have a series of talking heads.

1330
00:58:04.940 --> 00:58:10.480
First of all, Phyllis is going to let us know that she got the call from the, I guess,

1331
00:58:10.800 --> 00:58:13.400
DNA offices or adoption agency.

1332
00:58:13.400 --> 00:58:14.520
You know, the DNA offices.

1333
00:58:14.660 --> 00:58:14.940
You know.

1334
00:58:15.020 --> 00:58:16.000
They're by the DMV.

1335
00:58:16.240 --> 00:58:19.780
It's like post office, DMV, the DNA office.

1336
00:58:20.340 --> 00:58:20.520
Exactly.

1337
00:58:20.860 --> 00:58:24.360
Well, they called and she and Erin are not related.

1338
00:58:24.620 --> 00:58:26.260
But she's going to tell her another day.

1339
00:58:26.700 --> 00:58:26.940
Yeah.

1340
00:58:27.100 --> 00:58:27.280
Yeah.

1341
00:58:27.480 --> 00:58:30.820
They've been enjoying, I guess, this idea that maybe Phyllis is her mom.

1342
00:58:31.260 --> 00:58:37.360
And she also encouraged Erin to really go for Andy and Erin did it with a sock puppet

1343
00:58:37.360 --> 00:58:38.960
and was told no in front of everyone.

1344
00:58:38.960 --> 00:58:42.800
So maybe not the best day to get additional bad news.

1345
00:58:43.400 --> 00:58:44.240
Good point.

1346
00:58:44.880 --> 00:58:51.020
The episode ends with a bunch of talking heads from all the various candidates about, you

1347
00:58:51.020 --> 00:58:54.480
know, whether or not they think they're going to get this job as the manager.

1348
00:58:54.940 --> 00:58:57.300
They end with Finger Lakes guy.

1349
00:58:57.560 --> 00:59:01.700
We finally meet the guy who was so worried about getting the first two weeks off work

1350
00:59:01.700 --> 00:59:02.640
to go to the Finger Lakes.

1351
00:59:02.640 --> 00:59:03.880
And it's Jim Carrey.

1352
00:59:04.520 --> 00:59:08.780
Brent Forrester was the person in charge of reaching out to Jim Carrey's reps.

1353
00:59:08.780 --> 00:59:12.760
Brent said that Jim Carrey was an enthusiastic yes.

1354
00:59:13.100 --> 00:59:18.120
And incidentally, Jim Carrey received a nomination for favorite TV guest star at the

1355
00:59:18.120 --> 00:59:20.820
38th People's Choice Awards for this cameo.

1356
00:59:20.980 --> 00:59:22.320
Aw, for Finger Lakes guy?

1357
00:59:22.340 --> 00:59:23.600
For Finger Lakes guy.

1358
00:59:24.040 --> 00:59:27.220
So fun that we got all of these cool guest stars for this episode.

1359
00:59:27.220 --> 00:59:28.980
It really made it fun to rewatch.

1360
00:59:29.520 --> 00:59:32.840
Well, we have one final moment with Creed as branch manager.

1361
00:59:32.840 --> 00:59:35.480
He's talking to his ninth biggest client.

1362
00:59:36.140 --> 00:59:37.060
It's Pam.

1363
00:59:37.620 --> 00:59:38.060
Yes.

1364
00:59:38.320 --> 00:59:42.940
And he thinks the ninth biggest client and his fourth biggest client would get along.

1365
00:59:42.980 --> 00:59:44.980
And now they have to all talk to each other.

1366
00:59:45.360 --> 00:59:45.960
Yes.

1367
00:59:46.400 --> 00:59:50.900
So one of my favorite moments in this little bit, I improvised.

1368
00:59:51.860 --> 00:59:54.800
There's the moment when, you know, he says,

1369
00:59:55.160 --> 00:59:58.260
Hey, Jordan, patch through my fourth biggest client.

1370
00:59:58.800 --> 01:00:02.080
And I move the phone across my keyboard.

1371
01:00:02.480 --> 01:00:05.400
That was like, that's the patching through sound.

1372
01:00:05.740 --> 01:00:07.560
That was a little bit I came up with.

1373
01:00:07.900 --> 01:00:08.500
I loved it.

1374
01:00:08.660 --> 01:00:13.220
And then I got to perform both sides of the conversation, which was, I mean, it delighted me.

1375
01:00:13.680 --> 01:00:15.660
Well, I don't know if anyone else caught it.

1376
01:00:15.940 --> 01:00:20.140
But remember how Creed said he would intentionally say people's names wrong on purpose,

1377
01:00:20.300 --> 01:00:22.180
even if they were written correctly in the script?

1378
01:00:22.380 --> 01:00:22.640
Yes.

1379
01:00:22.980 --> 01:00:24.960
Well, in this scene, he called Jordan,

1380
01:00:25.340 --> 01:00:25.880
Jordana.

1381
01:00:26.260 --> 01:00:26.960
Oh, nice.

1382
01:00:28.220 --> 01:00:32.300
Well, we should say that this is going to end Creed's stint as manager.

1383
01:00:32.560 --> 01:00:35.640
And we'll also be saying goodbye to Cody Horn, who played Jordan.

1384
01:00:35.800 --> 01:00:37.340
She does not return in season eight.

1385
01:00:37.660 --> 01:00:40.960
But a lot of new stuff does happen in season eight.

1386
01:00:41.080 --> 01:00:43.880
And I cannot wait to break down the liSt.

1387
01:00:44.140 --> 01:00:45.240
Oh, I can't wait.

1388
01:00:45.440 --> 01:00:48.800
Before we get to season eight, we had a fun idea, you guys.

1389
01:00:48.800 --> 01:00:52.920
We think it is time to break down a Keanu Reeves movie.

1390
01:00:53.420 --> 01:00:55.220
And we're going to start with speed.

1391
01:00:55.220 --> 01:00:59.780
Yes, a little palate cleanser between season seven and season eight.

1392
01:00:59.960 --> 01:01:01.720
Next week, we're breaking down speed.

1393
01:01:02.060 --> 01:01:06.980
So tune in next week to hear us talk about Keanu Reeves and everything about that big old bus.

1394
01:01:06.980 --> 01:01:09.400
And thank you guys so much for listening today.

1395
01:01:09.640 --> 01:01:12.700
And a big thank you to Rainn Wilson, who came into this studio.

1396
01:01:13.720 --> 01:01:16.440
Just what a special person.

1397
